cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
title: "Tracing the piecemeal spread of crops into southern Africa: figure code and data"
abstract: >-
  R code and supporting data reproducing the main-text and supplementary
  figures of a study of archaeobotanical evidence for the arrival of introduced
  crops in southern Africa between 500 BCE and 1500 CE, including the data
  wrangling and the chronological rules that place each sample in a 500-year
  window.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Williams
    given-names: "Alice J."
    affiliation: "Research Laboratory for Archaeology and the History of Art, School of Archaeology, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX1 3QY, UK"
  - family-names: Jones
    given-names: "Mica B."
    affiliation: "Research Laboratory for Archaeology and the History of Art, School of Archaeology, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX1 3QY, UK"
  - family-names: Kapumha
    given-names: Russell
    affiliation: "Research Laboratory for Archaeology and the History of Art, School of Archaeology, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX1 3QY, UK"
  - family-names: Charles
    given-names: Michael
    affiliation: "School of Archaeology, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX1 2PG, UK"
  - family-names: Bogaard
    given-names: Amy
    affiliation: "School of Archaeology, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX1 2PG, UK"
  - family-names: Chirikure
    given-names: Shadreck
    affiliation: "Research Laboratory for Archaeology and the History of Art, School of Archaeology, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX1 3QY, UK"
